child actors have delivered some of the  most surprising and impressive  performances in hollywood history but  just because you were great doesn't mean  you'll be in the next terminator movie  did you notice the absence of these  actors from their sequels  in 1991 filmmaker james cameron  unleashed terminator 2 judgment day the  action-packed follow-up to his  comparatively low-budget 80s sci-fi  thriller at the heart of the blockbuster  sequel is the father-son relationship  between a young john connor and arnold  schwarzenegger's robotic killing machine  from the future and if you want to shine  them on it's hasta la vista baby  hasta la vista baby  connor played by a young edward furlong  in his first film role is destined to  lead a revolution against skynet in the  future so it only made sense that  furlong would return to reprise the role  in subsequent sequels 12 years later  however terminator 3 rise of the  machines was released with actor nick  stahl stepping up as humanity's savior  despite being the appropriate age for  the role furlong was replaced when  production began during a public  appearance in 2019 the actor who  struggled with substance abuse for many  years told an audience i was part of the  project and had a very nice deal but  then i guess to celebrate i went out and  overdosed on coke and kind of destroyed  that whole thing t2 would not be the  last time audiences saw furlong as conor  however the release of terminator dark  fate in 2019 had him briefly return as  the character through the power of  d-aging technology  the saga of rocky balboa began in 1976  with the release of rocky which was  written by its star sylvester stallone  the story of a nobody getting his chance  to take on the biggest name in boxing  was such a colossal success that the  series is still going strong today ena  freed and rocky krakoff appear as rocky  jr and rocky iii and rocky iv  respectively but it's sage stallone's  betrayal of rocky's son in the fifth  film that is most worthy of note since  he was the actual son of sylvester  stallone 16 years after the film's  release the italian stallion returned in  rocky balboa although he was the right  age to return as robert sage stallone  declined to participate in the 2006 film  instead milo ventimiglia became the  fourth actor to play rocky's son as it  turned out sage declined the role to  focus on his career behind the scenes in  2006 the same year rocky balboa was  released sage directed the award-winning  short film vic sadly the younger  stallone passed away in 2012.  following the release of the  ill-received halloween three season of  the witch the halloween series was  rejuvenated with halloween for the  return of michael myers this time the  story focused on jamie lloyd who lives  with the foster family after the death  of her mother lori strode lloyd  portrayed by child actor danielle harris  returned the following year for  halloween five the revenge of michael  myers when the sixth film the curse of  michael myers was released in 1995 lloyd  was played by actress jc brandy instead  harris had planned on playing jaime  again but the producers originally  decided not to hire her because she was  just 17 years old at the time in a later  interview harris explained that the  producers wanted someone who was 18  freeing the production team to work more  hours on set consequently if she wanted  the role she would have had to become  emancipated surprisingly harris actually  agreed to go through this process only  to discover that the movie was turning  into something she didn't agree with one  particular meeting with producers about  the new script raised doubts about the  project in her mind harris explained i  remember leaving thinking oh these  people don't know halloween so i'm  pregnant with my uncle's baby like i  just didn't understand what had shifted  she was also told that her character  wasn't important enough to pay her the  salary she felt she deserved especially  after going through so many hurdles to  take the role in the first place in the  end she stepped away from the project  altogether  leonardo dicaprio has been very famous  for a very long time in 1997 he became a  superstar following the release of  titanic and he has worked steadily over  the years even winning an oscar for his  performance in 2015's the revenant but  one of his very first credits was a  horror movie 1991's critters 3 the third  installment of the cult horror series  from new line cinema dicaprio played the  stepson of the greedy landlord of a cd  apartment building in which the  protagonists of the film reside and less  than a year after the release of  critters 3 critters 4 was released but  this time without dicaprio dicaprio's  lack of involvement in the movie doesn't  appear to have anything to do with the  desire to recast the story simply didn't  allow for the inclusion of the character  from critters 3 as the narrative jumped  ahead to the year 2045. then again  dicaprio probably wasn't too devastated  about this considering he received his  first academy award nomination for  what's eating gilbert grape just two  years later  not only were the home alone movies  gigantic hit to the box office but the  first film released in 1990 also  launched its 10 year old lead into mega  stardom the little troublemaker with a  heart of gold and a penchant for  violence made macaulay culkin so famous  that he started popping up pretty much  everywhere oh mac here have a sprite  the staggering success of both home  alone and home alone 2 lost in new york  spurred production on a third movie and  in 1997 home alone 3 was released only  this time the spunky blonde kid  defending his home from criminals was  not played by culkin but by alex d lin's  culkin's absence can be explained by his  semi-retirement from acting in 1994. the  mid-90s were a particularly difficult  time in culkin's personal life and he  likely wanted to step away from the  limelight for a little while he does  still feature in movies and tv shows  every now and again but these days he's  much more selective about the parts he  plays  barrett oliver was our original gateway  to the magical world of fantasia in the  cult classic movie the never-ending  story it was his sympathetic portrayal  of the lonely bullied bookworm bastion  bucks that taught generations of  dreamers to always keep your imagination  alive when the sequel the never-ending  story 2 the next chapter was released in  1990 however there were a number of  casting changes including that of the  protagonist 90s star jonathan brandis  was cast as bastion for the follow-up as  with macaulay culkin it appears as  though oliver did not return because he  left acting behind in 1989 since then  the former child actor has devoted his  life to photography specializing in 19th  century camera processes  few young actors in the 1980s were as  charismatic and lovable as corey feldman  and his popularity was reflected in the  sheer number of roles he took throughout  that decade in the mid 80s feldman was  cast as the monster obsessed youth tommy  jarvis in friday the 13th the final  chapter the fourth film in the slasher  series tommy's peculiar love of masks  serves him well during the final  confrontation with the monolithic killer  jason voorhees as he uses his talent for  makeup to transform himself into jason  as a child confusing the killer long  enough to take him down the film's final  scene however hints at more to come for  tommy although the character would face  off with jason twice more feldman would  only play him in a brief cameo on friday  the 13th a new beginning during an  interview in 2011 he talked about his  experiences working on the fourth film  explaining how his commitment to the  goonies prevented him from starring in a  new beginning by the time friday the  13th part 6 jason lives was released the  character of tommy jarvis had aged up  making it difficult to bring feldman  back for the role  aliens the sequel to ridley scott's  classic 1979 space horror jumped forward  even further into the future dropping  sigourney weaver's alan ripley character  into a strange and lonely new world even  worse the aliens that killed her crew  have now infested a human colony on the  moon from the original film forcing  ripley to join a team of space marines  to investigate what happened it's here  that she meets newt a human survivor  living and hiding from the xenomorphs  we better get back because it'll be dark  soon and they mostly come at night  mostly  newt was played by 10 year old newcomer  carrie hen she had never acted before  and it appeared as though she had a  bright future in acting ahead of her  however the young actress decided to  leave show business shortly after  finishing the film deciding instead to  focus on just being a kid in 2019 she  told avp galaxy about why she made her  decision her father had been stationed  in england where aliens was filmed but  was later transferred to california now  that she lived in the states again she  briefly considered going back to acting  but decided against it she explained i  wanted to be a normal child and i'd  lived in england since i was about two  so it was quite a culture shock coming  back to the states and especially coming  back to california being in a well-known  film and speaking with an accent made  adjusting difficult but she persevered  and went on to accomplish her lifelong  goal of becoming a teacher something she  continues to do to this day  movie audiences met the werewolf  heartthrob jacob black in 2008's mega  smash hit twilight for many film goers  this was their introduction to actor  taylor lautner who would go on to star  in subsequent twilight films as well as  2011's abduction before becoming a  leading man however loutner had been the  co-lead of a wild superhero film for  kids called the adventures of sharkboy  and lava girl 3d  although this 2005 film wasn't exactly a  huge success it did get a spin-off in  the 2020 netflix film we can be heroes  the netflix follow-up features a brief  appearance from sharkboy and lavagirl  but only lava girl's original actor  taylor dooley returned to her role  sharkboy was instead played by stuntman  jeff dashnot who had long been a  frequent collaborator with writer  director robert rodriguez when speaking  to yahoo entertainment rodriguez said  there was no reason to bring lautner  back as sharkboy he explained i wouldn't  see sharkboy's face because i wanted him  to be more like batman there wasn't  enough to bring taylor lautner on he's  such a big star now and for him to not  have any dialogue and have his face  covered fans would be in an uproar  stanley kubrick's adaptation of stephen  king's novel the shining was released in  1980 and although it is now remembered  as a classic of the horror genre it  didn't set the world on fire right away  one of the film's major critics was  stephen king himself who disagreed with  kubrick's interpretation of his novel  the film has only grown in his steam  over the decades however and is now  widely considered a masterpiece king  released a sequel novel dr sleep in 2013  and in 2019 the sequel was adapted into  film by director mike flanagan who  envisioned it as both an adaptation of  king's novel and as a direct sequel to  the kubrick film while five-year-old  danny lloyd played danny torrance in  1980 he only returned for a brief cameo  as an unrelated character at a baseball  game in dr sleep instead ewan mcgregor  was selected to play the adult dany in  the sequel the reason for this was very  simple danny lloyd gave up acting years  ago talking to the guardian lloyd  discussed his life as a biology  professor in kentucky and his decision  to leave acting after years of  auditioning lloyd decided to call it  quits in the industry he explained i  wouldn't say it was upsetting but as i  got a little bit older it kind of got  boring lloyd is now a father of four and  holds no regrets about his decision  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite movies are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]

